21. QUORUM

Quorum means:

Minimum number of members required to conduct business.

For either House of Parliament:

1/10 of the total number of members

Example:

If a House has 500 members:

500 ÷ 10 = 50

Quorum = 50.

22. ZERO HOUR

This is a favorite general-awareness concept.

Zero Hour is the period when members raise matters of urgent public importance.

Important:

Zero Hour is not mentioned in the Constitution.

It developed through parliamentary practice.

So if SSC asks:

Zero Hour is constitutionally mentioned?

Answer:

❌ No.

23. QUESTION HOUR

Question Hour is when members ask questions to ministers.

Purpose:

Parliamentary accountability

Example:

MP asks:

"How much money was spent on X scheme?"

Minister answers.

This allows Parliament to scrutinize the executive.

24. NO-CONFIDENCE MOTION

Very important.

A no-confidence motion tests whether the government still enjoys the confidence of:

Lok Sabha

If the government loses majority support in Lok Sabha, it may have to resign.

Memory

Confidence = Government = Lok Sabha

