Constant time.

Example:

printf("%d", a[3]);

One direct access.

O(n)

Linear.

Example:

for(i = 0; i < n; i++)

Runs approximately n times.

O(log n)

Repeatedly reduces the problem.

Classic example:

Binary search

If you have:

1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8

Binary search repeatedly halves the search space.

Therefore:

O(log n)

31. QUICK COMPARISON
Operation	Typical complexity
Array direct access	O(1)
Linear search	O(n)
Binary search	O(log n)
Nested loop n × n	O(n²)
