6. Q18 — Binary Search

You answered:

A. Linear search ❌

Correct:

B. Binary search

This is an important Computer Science concept.

Suppose we have:

1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8

Binary search checks the middle.

If the target is greater than the middle:

discard left half

If smaller:

discard right half

So:

8 elements
↓
4
↓
2
↓
1

The search space is repeatedly divided by 2.

Therefore:

Binary Search = O(log n)

Compare:
Search	Requirement	Complexity
Linear Search	No sorting required	O(n)
Binary Search	Sorted data required	O(log n)
Paper-I level

